4. GENERATOR CAPABILITY AND DISPATCH ARITHMETIC
==============================================================================
P at rated pf   = 458 * 0.85            = 389.3000 MW   (SIE PN = 389.30 MW)
Q at rated pf   = 458 * sin(acos(0.85)) = 241.2665 MVAr (APS Qmax = +241 MVAr)
  => APSCL's +241 MVAr is the stator limit AT P = 389.30 MW, not at 342.01 MW.
Workbook capacity B3 = 360 MW ; 360/458 = pf 0.78603 (a rating statement, not a dispatch)
APS "Site De-rated Active Power" = 342.01 MW ; 342.01/458 = pf 0.74675
SIE Smax = 518 MVA at 30 degC cold gas -> I at 22.0 kV = 13594.0 A (SIE Imax = 14309 A)
  apparent 5.00 % discrepancy. Test the -5 % voltage limit (22 kV -5 % = 20.9 kV):
  sqrt(3) * 20.9 kV * 14309 A = 517.98 MVA   (SIE Smax = 518 MVA)  error 0.003 %
  => Imax is quoted at the MINIMUM permitted terminal voltage, IN at nominal.
     Resolved internal consistency, NOT a source conflict.
  IN check: sqrt(3)*22 kV*12019 A = 457.99 MVA (nameplate SN = 458 MVA)

Dispatch cases (stator circle radius S_N = 458 MVA; Q_max = sqrt(S_N^2 - P^2)):
case     P (MW)  Qmax (MVAr)    S at Qmax         pf  source
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A        360.00       283.13       458.00    0.78603  WB B3 "Capacity (MW)"
B        389.30       241.27       458.00    0.85000  SIE PN = 458*0.85
C        342.01       304.62       458.00    0.74675  APS "Site De-rated Active Power"
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Q at rated pf (0.85) = 241.2665 MVAr applies ONLY to case B.
  NONE of these is a NET EXPORT figure: station auxiliaries and transformer
  losses have not been subtracted. Net export is a LOAD-FLOW RESULT (D2), not a datum.

