5b. WORKBOOK GSUT COLUMNS (AK3..AO3) vs THE CTI DATASHEET - WHERE REV2 GOT 16.63 %
==============================================================================
Workbook row 3 GSUT block: AK3=515 MVA, AL3=155.3 kW PNL, AM3=0.00034 INL,
                           AN3=1067.5 kW PFL, AO3=0.1663 %Z, AP3=YNd1, AQ3="Solid Ground".

(i) Impedance cell AO3 = 0.1663.
    CTI datasheet + SLD + SIE + APS all state Z = 16.0 % on 515 MVA.
    SIE 2.1.1 states the GENERATOR saturated xd = 166.3 % = 1.663 pu.
    AO3 = 0.1663 is 166.3 % / 1000, i.e. the generator reactance digits in the
    transformer impedance cell. Header AO2 itself says "(%Z or in pu)" - the unit
    is ambiguous in the source. Recorded as SOURCE_CONFLICT; 16.0 % adopted by
    hierarchy (tier-1 manufacturer datasheet over tier-3 collection sheet).

(ii) Copper loss implied by the workbook: AN3 - AL3 = 1067.5 - 155.3 = 912.2 kW
     R% = 100*912.2/515000 = 0.177126 %
     Rev2 hard-codes T.R1_pu_own = 0.001771 (rev2/data/ashuganj_rev2_registry.m:35).
     |R_wb - 0.1771 %| = 0.000026 % -> Rev2's GSUT R is DERIVED FROM THE WORKBOOK,
     not from the CTI datasheet.
     CTI loss table gives R = 0.212621 % and CTI states R = 0.21 % (agree to 1.25 %).
     Workbook route vs CTI stated: 15.65 % apart. CTI self-consistent, workbook is not.
     => adopt R = 0.21 %; record AL3/AN3 as SOURCE_CONFLICT (see (iii)).

(iii) No-load loss: AL3 = 155.3 kW vs CTI 159 kW (2.33 % apart).
      Total full-load loss: AN3 = 1067.5 kW vs CTI total at 515 MVA = 1282 kW (16.73 % apart).
      Rev2 Simulink Rm = 3316.5 comes from 515000/155.3 = 3316.2 (workbook), not 515000/159 = 3239.0 (CTI).

