6. GSUT MAGNETISING BRANCH - WHICH NO-LOAD CURRENT IS PHYSICALLY POSSIBLE?
==============================================================================
Rm(pu, own base) = S_rated/P_noload ; Lm(pu) = 1/sqrt(I0^2 - (1/Rm)^2)
Rm = 515 MVA / 159 kW = 3238.9937 pu ; 1/Rm = 3.087379e-04 pu = 0.030874 %
  CTI 0.13 % (datasheet, 100 % V)                I0=0.0013000 pu  radicand=+1.594681e-06  Lm=    791.89 pu
  WB AM3 read as pu (0.00034 pu = 0.034 %)       I0=0.0003400 pu  radicand=+2.028093e-08  Lm=   7021.92 pu
  WB AM3 read literally as 0.00034 %             I0=0.0000034 pu  radicand=-9.530751e-08  Lm=IMAGINARY -> IMPOSSIBLE
  => the literal 0.00034 % reading is falsified by physics (I0 < I_Rm), independently
     of any source hierarchy. 0.13 % (CTI) is adopted; WB AM3 recorded as SOURCE_CONFLICT.

